 executed prefill time/calls and no PP rate. An EOS decode may have no confirmed
 output while retaining its actual call time. Invalid phase records are refused
 before a summary or graph is written.
+
+The model owner also exposes `prefill_executor_ns` and `decode_executor_ns`
+in `lie_core_info`. Each completed prefill call adds its duration once; each
+native decode dispatch adds its duration once, even when it serves several
+rows. The core benchmark takes before/after deltas for a cohort. Serial
+prefill rate divides all physically executed prompt tokens by the prefill
+delta; native batch decode rate divides all confirmed output tokens by the
+decode delta. The latter is not the sum of overlapping per-job decode times.
+Both executor rates exclude admission, queue, rendering and client delivery.
+The separate output-over-complete-wall rate includes those costs.
 
 The direct `single`/`multi`/`fresh` benchmark records `timing_clock` as
 `CLOCK_MONOTONIC`. A sample carries `sample_begin_monotonic_ns`,
